From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:06:10 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-tg16

TurboGrafx-16 and PC Engine HuCards get their own shelf, Games/TG16, on
Beetle PCE Fast (mednafen_pce_fast) alone, with every platform policy
answered explicitly and its own Screen section: a Shader row on the
retro list, stored in Config/tg16_shader.txt, and a Picture row, Crop by
default, then Stretch and Actual, in Config/picture.txt. There is no PAL
Speed row: the system is 60 Hz only and 59.82 fps is inside the 2 fps
window. Only .pce is a game (no .sgx, no CD images); the title is the
file stem. The canvas is the SNES 360x240 one, Crop takes 8 lines off
the top and bottom, and Stretch follows the frame width when a game
switches dot clock. X and Y are slot's turbo, L1 and R1 the picture, L2
and R2 slot's. Saves, States and Labels get a TG16 folder. The shelf
shows the Sega Card shape until the HuCard lands.

The Screen page layout follows nelynes/slotPlus 92b7022 (GPL-3.0).
